.SS Configuration
.TP
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rustyfi/config.toml ", " ~/.config/rustyfi/config.toml
Your own settings; `$RUSTYFI_CONFIG_DIR` overrides where this is looked for.
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/rustyfi/config.toml
The defaults shipped with the install, found as
.IR <executable>/../share/rustyfi .
Consulted last, so a config you wrote always wins.
.SH STAGING
A program runs in two stages. Stage 1 is the document stage, which produces the
PDF and is where a
.I .saty
file's own code lives; stage 0 runs before it and builds stage-1 code.
.B &e
quotes: it does not run
.IR e ,
it yields a value standing for it.
.B ~e
splices, running
.I e
one stage earlier and inserting the resulting code value at that point. The two
are inverses. A quote is legal only at stage 0, a splice only at stage 1, and a
stage-0 binding cannot be named from stage 1: only
.B persistent
crosses.
.PP
SATySFi 0.0 declares one stage per file, with a
.BI @stage: " persistent|0|1"
header; 0.1 declares it per binding, as
.B val ~x
(stage 0) or
.B val persistent ~x
(persistent), a plain
.B val x
being stage 1. The type a quote produces is written
.BI code " <type>"
in 0.1, which 0.0 has no spelling for.
.PP
One deviation from upstream: upstream resolves every splice in a preprocessing
pass before any stage-1 code runs, whereas here a splice runs where it stands.
The value is the same for pure code-building; the two differ only for side
effects interleaved with stage-1 code.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT
Library root, when
.B \-\-lib\-root
is not given.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_FONT_DIR
Font root, when
.B \-\-font\-dir
is not given.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base of the compile-cache directory.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_OFFLINE
Make the package manager fail cleanly instead of reaching the network.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_REGISTRY_TOKEN
Bearer token for registry tarball downloads over HTTP.
.SH FILES
When no root is named, ALL of these are searched, in this order, from the
document's own directory (or, for
.BR satyrographos ,
the working directory) upward and then outward \(em so a project-local root
adds to the wider ones rather than replacing them. Naming a root with
.B \-\-lib\-root
or
.B $RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT
searches that one alone.
.TP
.I <dir>/lib\-rustyfi/
A checked-out source tree \(em development.
.TP
.I <dir>/.rustyfi/
A project-local root, recognised only where a
.I Satyristes
sits beside it.
.TP
.I <prefix>/lib/rustyfi
The install this binary belongs to, found as
.IR <executable>/../lib/rustyfi ,
so an unpacked archive works wherever it sits.
.TP
.IR ~/.local/lib/rustyfi ", " /usr/local/lib/rustyfi ", " /usr/lib/rustyfi
User-wide, then system-wide \(em where a release archive unpacks to.
.PP
Inside whichever root is chosen:
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/packages/
SATySFi 0.0 packages.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist\-v01/packages/
SATySFi 0.1 packages.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/fonts/
Bundled font files, each with its licence beside it.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/hash/fonts.rustyfi\-hash
Maps a font name used by a document to the file that provides it;
.I default\-font.rustyfi\-hash
names the regular, bold, oblique and math defaults.
.TP
.I <doc>.satysfi\-aux
Cross-reference table, in the same JSON format upstream SATySFi writes, so the
two interoperate.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non-zero if the document fails to load, typecheck, evaluate or
render, or if a package operation fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile a document with the packages and fonts from an unpacked release:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ export RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT=/opt/rustyfi/lib/rustyfi
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-o doc.pdf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview the same layout in a browser, and see where the time goes:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-format html
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-timing
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and manual, and upstream SATySFi:
.UR https://github.com/gfngfn/SATySFi
.UE .
.SH LICENSE
MIT. The bundled fonts keep their own licences, which travel beside them in
.IR <lib\-root>/dist/fonts/ ,
and the SATySFi packages under
.I <lib\-root>
are upstream's, under the LGPL-3.0.
